    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Ectopic lymph node was considered — “Based on clinical and radiographic findings, a provisional diagnosis of ectopic lymph node and lipoma was made.”\n2. Lipoma was considered — “Based on clinical and radiographic findings, a provisional diagnosis of ectopic lymph node and lipoma was made.”\n3. Keloid was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes keloid…”\n4. Mucocele was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes keloid, mucocele, salivary gland tumour…”\n5. Salivary gland tumour (e.g., canalicular adenoma) was included — “The differential diagnosis includes…salivary gland tumour (such as canalicular adenoma arising from a minor salivary gland in the lip)…”\n6. Neurilemmoma was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…neurilemmoma…”\n7. Neurofibroma was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…neurofibroma (which might mimic angioleiomyoma clinically but has different IHC features)…”\n8. Granular cell tumour was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…granular cell tumour.”\n9. Angiomyolipoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as angiomyolipoma…”\n10. Myopericytoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as…myopericytoma…”\n11. Leiomyosarcoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as…leiomyosarcoma.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\nDiagnosis: Ectopic lymph node\nEvidence: The patient's presentation of a solitary, mobile, submucosal mass with ill-defined borders and a smooth mucosal surface, along with ultrasonography showing a well-d