l — “The differential diagnosis includes keloid, mucocele, salivary gland tumour…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"mucocele.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of mucocele.\n\nGroundtruth 5: Salivary gland tumour (e.g., canalicular adenoma) was included — “The differential diagnosis includes…salivary gland tumour (such as canalicular adenoma arising from a minor salivary gland in the lip)…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"salivary gland tumour\" or \"canalicular adenoma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of salivary gland tumour.\n\nGroundtruth 6: Neurilemmoma was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…neurilemmoma…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"neurilemmoma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of neurilemmoma.\n\nGroundtruth 7: Neurofibroma was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…neurofibroma (which might mimic angioleiomyoma clinically but has different IHC features)…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"neurofibroma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of neurofibroma.\n\nGroundtruth 8: Granular cell tumour was included in the differential — “The differential diagnosis includes…granular cell tumour.”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"granular cell tumour.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of granular cell tumour.\n\nGroundtruth 9: Angiomyolipoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as angiomyolipoma…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"angiomyolipoma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of angiomyolipoma.\n\nGroundtruth 10: Myopericytoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as…myopericytoma…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"myopericytoma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of myopericytoma.\n\nGroundtruth 11: Leiomyosarcoma was considered as a histologic mimic — “angiomyoma may exhibit morphological similarities with various benign and malignant soft tissue tumors, such as…leiomyosarcoma.”\n*   Potential match from Predicted: No statement in the predicted reasons mentions \"leiomyosarcoma.\"\n    *   Pros: None.\n    *   Cons: No direct mention of leiomyosarcoma.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth 1 matches with the predicted statement about ectopic lymph node.\n- Groundtruth 2 matches with the predicted statement about lipoma.\n- Groundtruth 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, and 11 have no matches in the predicted reasons.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"The patient's presentation of a solitary, mobile, submucosal mass with ill-defined borders and a smooth mucosal surface, along with ultrasonography showing a well-defined, hypoechoic lesion, is consistent with an ectopic lymph node.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [\n      \"The clinical findings of a submucosal mass with a smooth mucosal surface could also be indicative of a lipoma, although the presence of severe pain is less typical for this condition.\"\n    ],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [],\n    \"5\": [],\n    \"6\": [],\n    \"7\": [],\n    \"8\": [],\n    \"9\": [],\n    \"10\": [],\n    \"11\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
