a distended uterine cavity with fluid and air forming an air-fluid level, are consistent with an infected hematometra.\"\n     - Pros: This statement explicitly mentions \"infected hematometra\" and provides supporting evidence, which aligns with the groundtruth's suspicion of infected hematometra.\n     - Cons: None. This is a direct and strong match.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4: Consideration of tubo-ovarian abscess — “CT scan revealed a cystic multilocular left adnexa lesion with thick septa and solid intra-lesion component suspected of tubo-ovarian abscess.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not mention tubo-ovarian abscess.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 5: Consideration of benign adnexal masses — “Benign adnexal masses … are gynecological cases resulting in chronic pelvic mass.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. While leiomyoma is a benign gynecological mass, the predicted reasons don't use the general term \"benign adnexal masses\" as a diagnostic consideration.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 6: Consideration of endometriosis — “Symptoms may mimic endometriosis in the pelvis.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Endometriosis is not mentioned.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 7: Consideration of primary ovarian neoplasms — “primary ovarian neoplasms are gynecological cases resulting in chronic pelvic mass.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Primary ovarian neoplasms are not mentioned.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 8: Consideration of colorectal masses — “Colorectal masses … are non-gynecologic causes.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Colorectal masses are not mentioned.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 9: Consideration of hematoma — “Colorectal masses, hematoma, and soft tissue tumors are non-gynecologic causes.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Hematoma is not mentioned in the context of a differential diagnosis.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 10: Consideration of soft tissue tumors — “Colorectal masses, hematoma, and soft tissue tumors are non-gynecologic causes.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Soft tissue tumors are not mentioned.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 11: Consideration of teratoma — “Teratoma and schwannoma can be differentiated by tumor markers Alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) and CA-125, whereas schwannoma is suspected if these tumor markers are negative.”\n   - No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. Teratoma or schwannoma are not mentioned.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth Reason 1 matches with the predicted reason discussing \"leiomyoma with cystic degeneration.\"\n- Groundtruth Reason 3 matches with the predicted reason discussing \"infected hematometra.\"\n- All other groundtruth reasons have no direct matches in the predicted reasons.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"The patient's history of progressive abdominal enlargement, difficulty with defecation and voiding, and the presence of a smooth, firm pelvic mass on rectovaginal examination, along with imaging findings of a large hypoechoic mass within the uterine cavity and a separate solid mass in the left adnexa, are consistent with a large uterine leiomyoma with cystic degeneration.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [\n      \"The patient's symptoms of brown-yellowish vaginal discharge, fluctuating lower abdominal pain, fever, and the imaging findings of a distended uterine cavity with fluid and air forming an air-fluid level, are consistent with an infected hematometra.\"\n    ],\n    \"4\": [],\n    \"5\": [],\n    \"6\": [],\n    \"7\": [],\n    \"8\": [],\n    \"9\": [],\n    \"10\": [],\n    \"11\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
