  "14dd78e46c9b6d997e1e6ad211effb2c54661e7d85a3af96931d134e69e29e6a": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Solid oral leiomyoma — “Microscopically, LLH should be differentiated from a solid oral leiomyoma … which is a true neoplasm of smooth-muscle origin, which is rare in the oral cavity.”\n2. Angiomyoma (vascular leiomyoma) — “Microscopically, LLH should be differentiated from … an angiomyoma (angioleiomyoma; vascular leiomyoma).”\n3. Lipoma — “Other lesions that have a similar clinical presentation such as a lipoma … should likewise be considered.”\n4. Granular cell tumor — “Other lesions that have a similar clinical presentation such as … granular cell tumor … should likewise be considered.”\n5. Choristoma — “Other lesions that have a similar clinical presentation such as … choristoma … should likewise be considered.”\n6. Fibrous epithelial polyp — “Other lesions that have a similar clinical presentation such as … fibrous epithelial polyp … should likewise be considered.”\n7. Benign mesenchymoma — “Other lesions that have a similar clinical presentation such as … benign mesenchymoma … should likewise be considered.”\n8. Vascular or lymphatic lesions — “As the appearance of LLH can be nonspecific, other lesions such as vascular or lymphatic lesions … should not be neglected.”\n9. Mucus extravasation phenomena — “As the appearance of LLH can be nonspecific, other lesions such as … mucus extravasation phenomena … should not be neglected.”\n10. Reactive or traumatic lesions — “As the appearance of LLH can be nonspecific, other lesions such as … reactive or traumatic lesions … should not be neglected.”\n11. Benign or malignant neoplasm — “As the appearance of LLH can be nonspecific, other lesions such as … benign or malignant neoplasm … should not be neglected.”\n12. Cystic lesions — “As the appearance of LLH can be nonspecific, other lesions such as … cystic lesions should not be neglected.”\n13. Lingual thyroid — “In a paediatric population, hamartomas should be differentiated from lingual thyroid