m Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    - The predicted reasons do not mention vegetation.\n\nAnalysis of Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4: Metastatic tumors — “The differential diagnosis for intracardiac masses includes … metastatic tumors…”\n- Potential matches from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    - The predicted reasons do not specifically mention metastatic tumors. While \"other primary benign or malignant tumors\" (Groundtruth 5) is a broader category, \"metastatic tumors\" is distinct enough to require a specific mention if present.\n\nAnalysis of Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 5: Other primary benign or malignant tumors — “The differential diagnosis for intracardiac masses includes … other primary benign or malignant tumors.”\n- Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n    - \"The mass is attached to the interventricular septum with focal contrast enhancement, which could also be consistent with a papillary fibroelastoma.\"\n        - Pros: Papillary fibroelastoma is a type of primary benign cardiac tumor, fitting the \"other primary benign or malignant tumors\" category.\n        - Cons: The predicted reason is very specific to papillary fibroelastoma, whereas the groundtruth is a broad category. However, it does represent an \"other primary benign tumor.\"\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth 1 (\"Myxoma\") matches Predicted Reason 1 (\"The patient has a mobile, smooth, oval, pedunculated mass originating from the left ventricular lateral wall, which is consistent with a cardiac myxoma.\").\n- Groundtruth 2 (\"Thrombus\") has no match.\n- Groundtruth 3 (\"Vegetation\") has no match.\n- Groundtruth 4 (\"Metastatic tumors\") has no match.\n- Groundtruth 5 (\"Other primary benign or malignant tumors\") matches Predicted Reason 2 (\"The mass is attached to the interventricular septum with focal contrast enhancement, which could also be consistent with a papillary fibroelastoma.\") because papillary fibroelastoma is a type of primary benign tumor.\n\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"The patient has a mobile, smooth, oval, pedunculated mass originating from the left ventricular lateral wall, which is consistent with a cardiac myxoma.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [],\n    \"5\": [\n      \"The mass is attached to the interventricular septum with focal contrast enhancement, which could also be consistent with a papillary fibroelastoma.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```",
