d in light of progressive soft-tissue enlargement but was excluded by histopathology showing benign fibrofatty proliferation: “suggesting a lipofibroma” without atypia.\n- No direct match in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not discuss the consideration or exclusion of soft tissue sarcoma or histopathology findings.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1, \"The CT scan shows overgrowth of phalanges and surrounding soft tissue, suggesting a lipomatous process, which is consistent with lipofibromatous hamartoma\" is a partial match. While the groundtruth is using the CT findings to *exclude* a specific subtype of lipofibromatous hamartoma, the predicted reason uses the same CT findings to *support* the broader diagnosis of lipofibromatous hamartoma. The description of the CT findings themselves is consistent.\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2, there are no matches.\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 3, there are no matches.\n- For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4, there are no matches.\n\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"The CT scan shows overgrowth of phalanges and surrounding soft tissue, suggesting a lipomatous process, which is consistent with lipofibromatous hamartoma.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```",
