r malignancy.\n        *   Pros: This statement provides evidence for colorectal cancer, which aligns with the diagnosis in the groundtruth. It describes findings suspicious for malignancy in the colon.\n        *   Cons: The specific evidence (CT findings) is different from the immunohistochemical markers mentioned in the groundtruth statement. However, both support the idea of colorectal cancer.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2: Primary gastrointestinal neuroendocrine tumour — “Although neuroendocrine tumours can arise in any body region 95% of all small cell carcinomas are lung origin…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    *   Pros: No statements in the predicted reasons mention neuroendocrine tumors, small cell carcinomas, or lung origin.\n    *   Cons: No relevant terms or concepts are present in the predicted reasons.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 3: Metastatic Merkel cell carcinoma — “Metastatic Merkel cell carcinoma is considered less likely as there is no cytoplasmic CK20 staining.”\n*   Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    *   Pros: No statements in the predicted reasons mention Merkel cell carcinoma, metastasis, or CK20 staining.\n    *   Cons: No relevant terms or concepts are present in the predicted reasons.\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 4: Metastatic small cell carcinoma of lung — “positive immunostaining for TTF1 with negative staining for Caudal-type Homeobox 2 (CDX2) lead us to suspect a lung origin tumour…”\n*   Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons: None.\n    *   Pros: No statements in the predicted reasons mention small cell carcinoma, lung origin, TTF1, or CDX2 in this context.\n    *   Cons: No relevant terms or concepts are present in the predicted reasons.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n\n*   For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1 (\"Primary colorectal adenocarcinoma — “primary colorectal tumours tend to demonstrate the opposite pattern being positive for CDX2 and negative for TTF1…”\"), I will match Predicted Diagnostic Reason 3 (\"Diagnosis: Colorectal cancer\") and Predicted Diagnostic Reason 4 (\"Evidence: The patient had a thickened, woody sigmoid colon and mural thickening of the cecum and sigmoid colon on CT scan, which are suspicious for malignancy.\"). Both directly relate to the diagnosis of colorectal cancer, even if the specific evidence differs.\n*   For Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 2, 3, and 4, there are no matching statements in the Predicted Diagnostic Reasons.\n\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"Diagnosis: Colorectal cancer\",\n      \"Evidence: The patient had a thickened, woody sigmoid colon and mural thickening of the cecum and sigmoid colon on CT scan, which are suspicious for malignancy.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```",
