auses, such as Duane syndrome, Brown’s syndrome, and CFEOM.”\n- Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n    - 2. The presence of a right orbital linear soft-tissue lesion medial to the medial rectus muscle, with characteristics similar to extraocular muscle, could be related to an abnormality in the superior oblique tendon, which is a feature of Brown syndrome.\n        - Pros: The ground truth explicitly lists \"Brown's syndrome\" as a congenital cause. The predicted reason directly mentions \"Brown syndrome\" and links a finding to it.\n        - Cons: The predicted reason focuses on Brown syndrome specifically, while the ground truth lists it among other congenital syndromes. However, it is a direct mention of one of the syndromes listed.\n- Decision: Match with Predicted Diagnostic Reason 2.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth 1 (Cranial nerve palsy): No match.\n- Groundtruth 2 (Schwannoma): No match.\n- Groundtruth 3 (Thyroid eye disease): No match.\n- Groundtruth 4 (Orbital mass): Matches Predicted Diagnostic Reason 2.\n- Groundtruth 5 (Intracranial mass lesion): No match.\n- Groundtruth 6 (Congenital syndromes (Duane syndrome, Brown’s syndrome, CFEOM)): Matches Predicted Diagnostic Reason 2.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [\n      \"The presence of a right orbital linear soft-tissue lesion medial to the medial rectus muscle, with characteristics similar to extraocular muscle, could be related to an abnormality in the superior oblique tendon, which is a feature of Brown syndrome.\"\n    ],\n    \"5\": [],\n    \"6\": [\n      \"The presence of a right orbital linear soft-tissue lesion medial to the medial rectus muscle, with characteristics similar to extraocular muscle, could be related to an abnormality in the superior oblique tendon, which is a feature of Brown syndrome.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```",
