  "40ebe2a77a0a2a5a6a97be92b9d970772f0307d900271cd49ca3bcf27206224a": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Upper urinary tract urothelial carcinoma was suspected because “Typical symptoms are gross hematuria (80%) and flank pain (30%)” and imaging showed “a tubular filling defect with partial obstruction of the right mid ureter.”\n2. Ureteral fibroepithelial polyp was considered given that “IVU or retrograde pyelography typically demonstrates a tubular filling defect. This finding combined with negative cytology and biopsy should suspect a UFP.”\n3. Other benign ureteral lesions, including endometriomas, fibromas, leiomyomas, granulomas, neurofibromas, hemangiomas, and lymphangiomas, were contemplated because “Other benign lesions of the upper urinary tract include endometriomas, fibromas, leiomyomas, granulomas, neurofibromas, hemangiomas, and lymphangiomas.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. The patient's presentation with gross hematuria and intermittent right pelvic pain, combined with the finding of a pedunculated ureteral tumor on flexible ureteroscopy, is consistent with a ureteral fibroepithelial polyp, which is a benign tumor that can cause obstructive symptoms and bleeding.\n2. The patient's history of smoking and the presence of a tubular mass in the mid ureter on retrograde ureteropyelography could suggest a ureteral papilloma, which is a rare benign tumor that can cause hematuria and obstructive symptoms.\n\nAnalysis of Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1: \"Upper urinary tract urothelial carcinoma was suspected because “Typical symptoms are gross hematuria (80%) and flank pain (30%)” and imaging showed “a tubular filling defect with partial obstruction of the right mid ureter.”\"\n- Potential match 1 (Predicted 1): \"The patient's presentation with gross hematuria and intermittent right pelvic pain, combined with the finding of a pedunculated ureteral tumor on flexible ureteroscopy, is consistent with a ureteral fibroepithelial polyp, which is a benign tumor that can cause obstructive 