tatic seeding in the form of carcinomatosis omental.”\"\n    No direct matches in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not mention omental changes or peritoneal carcinomatosis.\n\nFor Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 5: \"Malignancy was questioned when fluid cytology showed no malignant cells — “Cytologic examination of pleural fluid showed lymphocytes, leukocytes, and mesothelial cells with no presence of malignant cells.”\"\n    No direct matches in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not mention fluid cytology or the absence of malignant cells.\n\nFor Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 6: \"Tuberculous lymphadenitis was identified on lymph-node biopsy — “the biopsy showed tubercles surrounded by lymphocytes... the pathological anatomy report concluded the diagnosis as tuberculous lymphadenitis.”\"\n    No direct matches in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not mention tuberculosis or lymphadenitis.\n\nFor Groundtruth Diagnostic Reason 7: \"Abdominal tuberculosis was confirmed by laparoscopy and biopsy showing granulomas — “Omentum biopsy revealed granuloma containing epithelioid cells and Langhans-type cells. These results suggested tuberculosis infection of omentum and liver.”\"\n    No direct matches in Predicted Diagnostic Reasons. The predicted reasons do not mention tuberculosis, laparoscopy, or granulomas.\n\nSummary of final matching decisions:\n- Groundtruth 1 matches Predicted Reason 1 (for adnexal thickening) and Predicted Reason 2 (for elevated CA-125).\n- Groundtruth 2 matches Predicted Reason 2 (for absence of mass on ultrasound).\n- Groundtruth 3 has no match.\n- Groundtruth 4 has no match.\n- Groundtruth 5 has no match.\n- Groundtruth 6 has no match.\n- Groundtruth 7 has no match.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"The patient's symptoms, lab results, and imaging studies suggest a malignancy, and the PET-CT showing FDG-avid thickening of bilateral adnexa suspicious for primary ovarian malignancy supports this diagnosis.\",\n      \"The patient's elevated CA-125 level, ascites, and pleural effusions are consistent with ovarian cancer, and the absence of a clear mass on ultrasound does not rule out this diagnosis, as some ovarian cancers can present with normal-sized ovaries.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [\n      \"The patient's elevated CA-125 level, ascites, and pleural effusions are consistent with ovarian cancer, and the absence of a clear mass on ultrasound does not rule out this diagnosis, as some ovarian cancers can present with normal-sized ovaries.\"\n    ],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": [],\n    \"5\": [],\n    \"6\": [],\n    \"7\": []\n  }\n}\n```\n</diagnostic_comparison>",
