  "ec4e8e61ad3807ecd615d993d1ced49444b41d1a4d187a90f401e0bb22503fdd": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. Phyllodes tumor was excluded by its characteristic pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia on histology — “glands were lined by bilayered epithelium with pericanalicular pattern of fibroadenoma and absence of cytological atypia.”\n2. Virginal hypertrophy was excluded by the finding of a discrete, well‐encapsulated tumor rather than diffuse glandular enlargement — “the specimen was sent for histopathological examination which showed well encapsulated tumor with hyperplasia of both epithelial and stromal components.”\n3. Adenocarcinoma was excluded by the absence of cytological atypia on histopathology — “absence of cytological atypia.”\n4. Tuberculosis was excluded by normal inflammatory markers and imaging — “Chest X-ray was normal.”\n\nPredicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n1. The patient's presentation of a rapidly enlarging, well-circumscribed, firm, and mobile breast lump, along with ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology results suggestive of fibroadenoma, supports this diagnosis.\n2. Although less likely, the large size and rapid growth of the breast mass could also be indicative of a phyllodes tumor, which can present similarly to fibroadenoma but often has a more variable and sometimes malignant course.\n\nAnalysis of potential matches:\n\nGroundtruth Diagnostic Reason 1: Phyllodes tumor was excluded by its characteristic pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia on histology — “glands were lined by bilayered epithelium with pericanalicular pattern of fibroadenoma and absence of cytological atypia.”\n*   Potential match from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons:\n    *   \"Although less likely, the large size and rapid growth of the breast mass could also be indicative of a phyllodes tumor, which can present similarly to fibroadenoma but often has a more variable and sometimes malignant course.\"\n        *   Pros: This predicted statement explicitly mentions