(BCC consideration for papules):\n- Potential match: Predicted Statement B.\n  - Pros: Both mention dermoscopic evaluation of papules showing features of BCC. Groundtruth: \"some papular lesions with the dermoscopic features of BCC.\" Predicted: \"Dermoscopic evaluation of the papules revealed features typical of basal cell carcinoma.\" Very close.\n  - Cons: None significant.\n  - Decision: Match.\n\n**Groundtruth Statement 3** (basosquamous carcinoma after immunohistochemistry):\n- No potential match in Predicted Statements.\n  - Predicted Statements do not mention basosquamous carcinoma, BerEP4, Bcl-2, or coexistence of squamous and basaloid components.\n  - Decision: No match.\n\n**Summary of Matching Decisions:**\n- Groundtruth 1 matches Predicted Statement A.\n- Groundtruth 2 matches Predicted Statement B.\n- Groundtruth 3 has no match.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [\n      \"Diagnosis: Invasive cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma\\nEvidence: The excisional biopsy of the lesion showed lobules and detached aggregates of eosinophilic keratinocytes with pleomorphic nuclei and prominent nucleoli infiltrating the reticular dermis, consistent with invasive cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma.\"\n    ],\n    \"2\": [\n      \"Diagnosis: Basal cell carcinoma\\nEvidence: Dermoscopic evaluation of the papules revealed features typical of basal cell carcinoma.\"\n    ],\n    \"3\": []\n  }\n}\n```",
