  "309ff4475a82a540f8faa17267fcb4d30b03daf8d7de82cab94564a078a36486": {
    "text": "<diagnostic_comparison>\n**Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons:**\n1. Phyllodes tumor was excluded by its characteristic pericanalicular fibroadenoma pattern and lack of atypia on histology — “glands were lined by bilayered epithelium with pericanalicular pattern of fibroadenoma and absence of cytological atypia.”\n2. Virginal hypertrophy was excluded by the finding of a discrete, well‐encapsulated tumor rather than diffuse glandular enlargement — “the specimen was sent for histopathological examination which showed well encapsulated tumor with hyperplasia of both epithelial and stromal components.”\n3. Adenocarcinoma was excluded by the absence of cytological atypia on histopathology — “absence of cytological atypia.”\n4. Tuberculosis was excluded by normal inflammatory markers and imaging — “Chest X-ray was normal.”\n\n**Predicted Diagnostic Reasons:**\n- Statement A (from fibroadenoma evidence): \"The patient's presentation of a rapidly enlarging, well-circumscribed, firm, and mobile breast lump, along with ultrasonography and fine-needle aspiration cytology results suggestive of fibroadenoma, supports this diagnosis.\"\n- Statement B (from phyllodes tumor evidence): \"Although less likely, the large size and rapid growth of the breast mass could also be indicative of a phyllodes tumor, which can present similarly to fibroadenoma but often has a more variable and sometimes malignant course.\"\n\n**Matching Analysis:**\n\n**Groundtruth Statement 1:** Excludes phyllodes tumor based on histology (pericanalicular pattern, bilayered epithelium, no atypia).\n- Potential match: Statement B mentions phyllodes tumor as a possibility, but does not exclude it; it actually suggests it could be considered. No mention of histology or exclusion criteria. No match.\n- Potential match: Statement A does not mention phyllodes tumor or histology. No match.\n- Decision: No match.\n\n**Groundtruth Statement 2:** Excludes virginal hypertrophy based on discrete encapsulated tumor vs diffuse enlargement.\n- Potential match: Statement A mentions \"well-circumscribed\" lump, but does not mention encapsulation or diffuse enlargement. No mention of virginal hypertrophy. No match.\n- Potential match: Statement B does not address virginal hypertrophy. No match.\n- Decision: No match.\n\n**Groundtruth Statement 3:** Excludes adenocarcinoma based on absence of cytological atypia.\n- Potential match: Neither statement mentions cytological atypia or adenocarcinoma. No match.\n- Decision: No match.\n\n**Groundtruth Statement 4:** Excludes tuberculosis based on normal chest X-ray.\n- Potential match: Neither statement mentions tuberculosis, inflammatory markers, or chest X-ray. No match.\n- Decision: No match.\n\n**Summary:** No statements from Predicted Diagnostic Reasons match any of the Groundtruth Diagnostic Reasons. All matching lists are empty.\n</diagnostic_comparison>\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matching_dict\": {\n    \"1\": [],\n    \"2\": [],\n    \"3\": [],\n    \"4\": []\n  }\n}\n```",
